  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRIB and Press TV operated in a dual register during September: domestically, both framed Iran's military operations as defensive responses to foreign aggression, and Araghchi's September 22–23 UNGA session as Tehran's participation in diplomacy from a position of strength. State media coverage of Rezaei's September 24 deadline statement — that the Strait would remain closed and talks would end unless Washington accepted Iran's seven conditions by approximately September 28–29 — led with the deadline as a demonstration of executive authority, not as a concession under pressure. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>

      <p>Armed Forces spokesman Abolfazl Shekarchi's September 16 statement that "200 nights of gatherings" had "disrupted the enemy's plans" placed pro-government rally coverage within a war-legitimacy narrative, presenting domestic mobilization as evidence of societal cohesion. IRIB ran footage of these demonstrations alongside combat coverage. Press TV carried an anonymous official statement asserting that "Iran will end the war when it decides to do so and when its own conditions are met." → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Pezeshkian's UNGA address was carried live and at length by IRIB. The defiant framing — "until our last breath," "we will not bow to bullying" — served a domestic audience navigating a contradiction: Iran was diplomatically engaged in New York but had not altered its conditions. IRIB did not carry Trump's "annihilate" threat in comparable depth; it presented the UNGA session as Iran placing its roadmap before the world body and Western delegations on its own terms. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

